>> title: Ham Sui Gok
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: pork, glutinous rice, chinese, deep-fry, dumpling
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: hom sui gok, haam seui gok, 鹹水角, fried pork dumpling, football dumpling, salty water dumpling
>> servings: 16
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the oil starts at 300°F and is eased up, and that order is the dish: dropped into hot oil the glutinous dough browns before it puffs, and it never gets the blistered shell. The filling is cooled first for the same reason every fried dumpling is
>> step.1: fry the pork and shrimp 5 min, cool 20 min
>> step.2: scald the wheat starch, knead the dough, rest 20 min
>> step.3: shape 16 footballs around the filling
>> step.4: fry 300°F (150°C) 6 min, easing the heat up

Fry @ground pork{8%oz}(225 g) with @dried shrimp{2%Tbs}(soaked and chopped), @dried shiitake mushrooms{2}(soaked and diced), @scallions{2}(sliced), @oyster sauce{1%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{2%tsp}, @sugar{1%tsp}, @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp} and @cornstarch{1%tsp}(slaked in 1 Tbs water) in a #wok{} for ~fry{5%min}, then spread it on a tray and ~cool{20%min}. A wet filling steams the dough open in the oil.

Stir @boiling water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) into @wheat starch{1/4%cup}(30 g) to a paste, then knead it together with @glutinous rice flour{2%cups}(280 g), @sugar{1/3%cup}(70 g), @lard{3%Tbs} and @warm water{1/2%cup}(120 mL) to a dough like soft putty and ~rest{20%min}.

Shape @&(~1)dough{} into 16 balls, flatten each one, close @&(~2)filling{} inside and work it into a pointed football between your palms.

Fry @&(~1)dumplings{} in @peanut oil{6%cups}(1.4 L; started at 300°F/150°C) for ~fry{6%min}, easing the heat up as they take colour, until they are blistered and deep gold. Sweet outside and salty inside is the whole point of the thing; a hot fryer splits them before the middle is even warm.
